+# Evidence register — GeoNerd competitive teardown
+
+- Idea: `geonerd`
+- Register opened: 2026-09-20
+- Method version: 1.0.0
+
+## Source
+
+- `/home/richard/projects/geonerd/docs/competitive-teardown.md` @ `327f02e`
+  (internal desk research, 197 lines, 2026-09-20).
+
+## Competitor map as recorded
+
+| Competitor | Positioning | Price (as recorded) | Threat |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| TendorAI | AI visibility for UK ICAEW/ACCA accountants; multi-surface scans, schema work | not recorded in source | High — same vertical, explicit accountant targeting |
+| SearchScore | Generic technical-readiness / AI tracking; 1,038 UK accountancy firms audited | from $25/mo | High — cheap, self-serve, already touching the vertical |
+| Tramwai | Free 12-area audit, done-for-you GEO retainer | £299/mo | Medium — different price tier; makes GeoNerd look cheap |
+| AireStream | GEO programme for UK professional services | not recorded | Medium |
+| Otterly.ai | Generic AI visibility tracker | $29/mo | Medium — commodity comparison point |
+| Free checkers (Ahrefs, Semrush, HubSpot) | Bundled visibility checks | £0 marginal | High — anchors "free" for measurement alone |
+
+## Interpretation used in scoring
+
+- A **defensible wedge** cannot be "first to accountants" — that position is
+  taken. The claimed wedge is vertical depth + honest measurement + plain-language
+  monthly actions at £19.99/mo.
+- The teardown is the strongest single source behind the `differentiation` score
+  and the main risk item in the dossier.
+- Prices and product claims are vendor marketing captured on an unrecorded date;
+  they may have changed. Re-verify before any launch decision.
+- The teardown was written by the same party as the product hypothesis; treat as
+  motivated research.
+
+## Related
+
+- `evidence/geonerd/2026-09-20-spike-findings.md`
+- `evidence/geonerd/2026-09-20-wedge-strategy.md`
